# ============================================
# apps/mobile/.env.example
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. NEVER commit the real .env (it is git-ignored).
#
# Expo loads .env when it starts (`pnpm dev:mobile`, `expo export`).
# - EXPO_PUBLIC_* are inlined into the app bundle at BUILD time and are PUBLIC:
#   anyone can read them from the installed app. Never put a secret here.
#   Validated by src/lib/env.ts; a missing/invalid value shows the app's
#   configuration error screen naming the variable.
# - MOBILE_* are read by app.config.ts on the build machine (app identity);
#   validated with zod, a wrong value stops `expo start` / `expo export`.
# See docs/technical/configuration/frontend.md and apps/mobile/README.md.
# ============================================

# ── Public (EXPO_PUBLIC_*) — bundled into the app ──

# REQUIRED outside development: the API's absolute https:// URL.
# In development (Expo Go) leave it unset: the app uses the dev machine's
# address that Expo Go connected to, plus EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT. Set it only to
# reach an API on another machine (http:// is allowed in development; an http://
# URL without a port gets EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT: http://192.168.1.5 → :8080).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# OPTIONAL (development only). The API's port: added to the dev machine's address,
# and to an http:// EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL that names no port. Default 8080.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=8080

# OPTIONAL, internal test builds ONLY. `true` puts the seeded quick sign-in
# buttons into a RELEASE build (development builds always have them). The demo
# passwords are then inside the APK: never set it for a build that leaves the
# team or goes to a store (ADR 042). `true`, `false` or unset; anything else
# is a configuration error.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SHOW_DEMO_ACCOUNT=true

# OPTIONAL, LAN test builds ONLY. `true` lets a RELEASE build use an http://
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL on a private LAN (10.x, 172.16-31.x, 192.168.x): a test APK
# for a phone on the same Wi-Fi (or hotspot) as this machine. Read at prebuild
# too (it allows plain http in the generated Android manifest), so run
# `expo prebuild` after changing it. Never for a build that leaves the team.
# See docs/technical/mobile/building-installable-apps.md §7.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ALLOW_LAN_HTTP_API=true

# OPTIONAL. Store pages the "Update required" screen opens (https only).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_IOS_STORE_URL=https://apps.apple.com/app/id0000000000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ANDROID_STORE_URL=https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.example.starter

# ── App identity (app.config.ts, build machine only) ──
# Products built on the starter rename the app here, never in code.

# OPTIONAL. Display name (max 30 characters). Default Starter.
# MOBILE_APP_NAME=Starter

# OPTIONAL. Expo slug: lower-case letters, digits and dashes. Default starter.
# MOBILE_APP_SLUG=starter

# OPTIONAL. iOS bundle identifier AND Android package: reverse-DNS segments of
# letters and digits (no dashes or underscores). Default com.example.starter.
# MOBILE_BUNDLE_ID=com.example.starter

# OPTIONAL. Deep-link URL scheme (Expo Router default links only). Default starter.
# MOBILE_SCHEME=starter
